jei.immersivenuclear.filter_press.info=3x3x9 multiblock (56 blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Slurry goes in at the front, on the pump end; the crude solution comes out at the front, on the other end; the residue comes out at the side, where the conveyor ends; energy on the heavy engineering blocks. At the back: filter input and spent filter output, to automate the swap. Needs all 28 filters. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
jei.immersivenuclear.filter.info=Filter of the Filtration Unit: the machine takes 28, one per plate. Every batch wears each filter by 1; a spent filter no longer filters and has to be replaced (in the interface or through the ports at the back).
jei.immersivenuclear.processing_reagent.info=Used by the Chemical Processing Unit, 16 per batch, with 16 uranium powder and 8000 mB of water.
jei.immersivenuclear.wet_mineral_residue.info=Solid residue of the Filtration Unit: the cake left between the plates, which falls when they open.
jei.immersivenuclear.uranium_slurry.info=Product of the Chemical Processing Unit; goes into the Filtration Unit.
jei.immersivenuclear.crude_uranium_solution.info=Product of the Filtration Unit: the uranium still dissolved with impurities. Goes on to the chemical separation (next machine).

